## 4. Vacancy Management API

The vacancy management system separates administrator operations from public vacancy access.

### Administrator endpoints

These endpoints are intended for authorised administrators.

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/admin/jobs` | Create a vacancy |
| `GET` | `/api/admin/jobs` | Retrieve vacancies for administration |
| `PATCH` | `/api/admin/jobs/{job_id}` | Update an existing vacancy |

Administrator requests must include the authentication credentials expected by the backend. Never expose administrator secrets in public website code or commit them to GitHub.

### Public endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/jobs` | Retrieve published public vacancies |
| `GET` | `/api/jobs/{job_id}` | Retrieve an individual public vacancy |

Public vacancy endpoints should return only vacancies that meet the backend's publication and visibility rules.

### Example API URLs

```text
GET https://averra-backend-dn23.onrender.com/api/jobs

GET https://averra-backend-dn23.onrender.com/api/jobs/1

GET https://averra-backend-dn23.onrender.com/api/admin/jobs

POST https://averra-backend-dn23.onrender.com/api/admin/jobs

PATCH https://averra-backend-dn23.onrender.com/api/admin/jobs/1
```

The example job ID `1` is illustrative; it does not imply that a vacancy with that ID exists.

